GT patch 0051: the fixed work every GE draw repeats before it joins a batch (docs/superpowers/specs/
2026-10-19-ge-backend-per-draw-cost-design.md). The UV range of a draw is four floats, not a zero-built ~600-byte
Batch; vertices and indices are appended with one resize; the merge test compares the descriptor around the four
per-draw fields instead of copying it; the framebuffer-feedback flag reuses the target lookup made at the top; the
fast path writes each vertex once and takes the strip indices of up to 8 vertices from a table. Output identical
(dual run over 16.8 M draws: vertices, indices, batches and counters equal).

